# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is the default on Windows checkouts, and it also rewrites
# files that `git archive` produces. A CRLF shell script unpacked on Linux fails
# on its first line ("set: pipefail: invalid option name"), and a CRLF
# Dockerfile or YAML entrypoint comment does the same inside a container -- so
# these formats are pinned to LF regardless of the host that packs them.
#
# Everything else is left alone: source files are already normalised by the
# checkout, and forcing LF on them would churn the tree for no gain.

*.sh           text eol=lf
Dockerfile*    text eol=lf
*.yml          text eol=lf
*.yaml         text eol=lf
